add('I08','I Repo and DevOps','Low','License and disclosure policy are absent','README.md','MIT License','README claims MIT but no tracked LICENSE; no SECURITY.md or format config. Root gitignore *.log also hides raw audit evidence unless explicitly force-added.','Tracked inventory has README claim but no license/security policy; frontend ESLint and strict TS configs do exist.','Add license with owner approval, security disclosure policy, formatter and documented explicit evidence tracking.')
add('A01','A Documentation','Medium','README and deployment guide describe obsolete identity and stack','README.md','Next.js 14','README claims Next14, custom JWT rotation, SWR and Llama3; manifests/code use Next16.2.4, Clerk, Zustand/local state/Axios and gpt-oss-20b. Deployment lists JWT secrets but not current Clerk/Redis/billing configuration. Clone URL is placeholder.','Compare manifests, auth middleware, ai.controller.ts and DEPLOYMENT.md against README lines. Frontend requires Node>=20.9, contrary to Node18+ prerequisite.','Rewrite onboarding from tested manifests and deploy target; unify identity, environment and migration instructions.')
add('A02','A Documentation','Medium','Feature and enterprise walkthrough claims exceed implementation','README.md','over 50 languages','Snippet UI offers 12 languages and plain escaped code without syntax highlighting. README role management UI is absent in settings, invitations require registered users. Walkthrough describes raw y-websocket and API-drained embeddings despite Hocuspocus/dedicated mismatched worker. It refers to two env examples; frontend example absent.','Compare snippets LANGUAGES and <code>, settings page, worker/service producer and tracked inventory. Backend .env.example exists; do not call it missing.','Maintain supported-feature matrix with limitations; add frontend env template and replace walkthrough protocol/worker/setup steps with verified operations.')
add('H08','H Frontend','High','Document upload sends bearer token to hardcoded localhost','frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/workspace/[id]/docs/page.tsx','fetch(`http://localhost:5000','Upload ignores configured API origin and always sends the Clerk bearer token to plaintext localhost:5000. Deployed users cannot ingest through the backend; any local listener receives that request/token if browser permits it.','Open ingestion UI from deployed origin: network target is user machine localhost, not NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL. Browser mixed-content/private-network behavior varies; successful token delivery unverified.','Use the centralized configured API client and secure deployment origin; test upload on real HTTPS deployment.')
add('A03','A Documentation','Medium','Landing page claims end-to-end encryption unsupported by data flow','frontend/src/app/page.tsx','End-to-End Encrypted','Document plaintext/JSON and Yjs bytes are available to the API/database; content is sent to AI providers. Repository secret encryption at rest does not provide end-to-end document encryption. Infinite scale and universally tenant-scoped workflow claims also exceed demonstrated behavior.','Inspect yjs persistence, content JSON, AI retrieval and D02/G08; no client document encryption/key exchange exists.','Remove unsupported encryption/scaling claims and publish an accurate trust/data-processing model.')
add('H09','H Frontend','Low','Light theme and toast color configuration conflict','frontend/src/app/globals.css','.dark, :root','Dark variables override :root unconditionally, so selecting light still retains dark base palette. Toaster wraps hex CSS variables in hsl(), producing invalid colors.','Toggle theme; class changes but :root still matches the later dark declaration. hsl(var(--card)) resolves to hsl(#0f1422).','Scope dark overrides to .dark and use var(--card) directly; verify both themes and contrast.')
add('H10','H Frontend','Low','Document templates omit template content','frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/workspace/[id]/docs/page.tsx','title: `${template.icon}','createFromTemplate passes title only, despite structured template content being defined above. createDocumentSchema does not accept content.','Select an ADR template: created document receives title but no template.content in request.','Version or extend create contract deliberately to accept validated initial content and initialize canonical CRDT once.')
add('D09','D Authorization','Medium','Task assignments accept users outside the workspace','backend/src/controllers/task.controller.ts','assigneeId,','Task create/update accepts any User ID; foreign key existence is the only assignment constraint, without checking WorkspaceMember.','As editor of A, submit assigneeId of user B who is not an A member. include assignee returns B name/avatar and causes activity attribution by the agent. Live reproduction requires isolated DB fixtures.','Require assignee membership in task workspace in the authorized transaction; validate removal/reassignment behavior.')
add('D10','D Authorization','Medium','Owner role updates can orphan a workspace','backend/src/controllers/workspace.controller.ts','data: { role: role as Role }','An owner can demote the last OWNER, including self; removal guard alone does not prevent an ownerless workspace and agent workflows depend on an OWNER.','PATCH own membership from OWNER to VIEWER when sole owner: no count/invariant check. Concurrent owner demotions also lack serialization.','Define owner-transfer policy and transactionally preserve at least one owner, with contention tests.')
add('I09','I Repo and DevOps','Low','Seed command refers to a missing file','backend/package.json','"db:seed"','db:seed executes prisma/seed.ts but no such file is tracked. Fresh seeded test/development setup is not reproducible.','Run npm run db:seed in an isolated installed copy: module cannot resolve missing seed.ts. Source inventory establishes absence.','Provide deterministic non-production seed fixtures and document their scope.')
counts=Counter(f['severity'] for f in F)
text='# Phase 0 audit\n\nAudit date: 2026-10-31. Source is the initial checkout on `main`, audited on `upgrade/enterprise`. No application code changes. Severity assesses impact if reachable, not proof of production compromise. Static confirmations are distinguished from unverified runtime consequences. No production credentials, accounts, exploit execution or external deployment were used.\n\n'
text+='## Summary\n\n| Severity | Findings |\n|---|---:|\n'+''.join(f'| {s} | {counts[s]} |\n' for s in ['Critical','High','Medium','Low'])+f'\nTotal: {len(F)} findings. Advisory counts are separate, not added to this table.\n\n'
text+='Critical priorities are host code execution, profile mass assignment, and document-room tenant confusion. Existing controls include Clerk verification, REST role checks on many routes, bounded HTTP JSON, upload size cap, Helmet, signed webhooks, encrypted repository secrets, parameterized SQL for user values, health/readiness endpoints, telemetry and graceful shutdown hooks. Claims that these controls are universally absent would be inaccurate.\n\n'
for area in sorted(set(f['area'] for f in F)):
 text+=f'## {area}\n\n'
 for f in [f for f in F if f['area']==area]:
  text+=f"### {f['id']} — {f['title']}\n\n- **Severity:** {f['severity']}\n- **File:line:** `{f['source']}`\n- **Status:** {f['status']}\n- **What is wrong:** {f['wrong']}\n- **Evidence / reproduction:** {f['evidence']}\n- **Recommended fix:** {f['fix']}\n\n"
text+='## Coverage and negative results\n\nAll tracked files are inventoried with hashes in `audit-evidence/source-inventory.json`; text/lockfile inventory is in `read-manifest.json`. Binary favicon was inventoried, not treated as text. Ignored generated dependencies and Git internals are outside source review. Nested `.kilo` worktree comparisons are recorded in scope.json and are not separate deployed application modules. No tracked actual provider secrets or build artifacts were identified; local ignored env files were reused only in ignored runtime copies and their values are intentionally absent from evidence. Git history was not exhaustively secret-scanned: historical exposure remains unverified.\n\nNo custom password hashing, refresh rotation/reuse detection, password reset or email verification implementation remains; Clerk owns those capabilities. Their configured strength, cookie flags, expiry, brute-force/MFA policy and server-side logout revocation cannot be proven without tenant dashboard access. There is no demonstrated localStorage auth-token persistence; IndexedDB does persist workspace content. Bearer authorization reduces ambient-cookie CSRF exposure on REST, but reset GET is a concrete exception. CORS is a fixed configured frontend origin with credentials; no wildcard is configured. Socket verifyToken calls do not specify authorizedParties; verify deployment origin/audience restrictions with issued tokens before claiming a cross-origin token vulnerability.\n\nNo raw SQL interpolation of request text through unsafe Prisma query APIs was found. Embedding vector uses Prisma.raw from provider numeric arrays, not direct user SQL; validate dimensions/numeric values. No accessible Cloudinary upload route or fetch-by-user-URL SSRF was found; the native runner already permits arbitrary network access. No proven prototype-pollution path identified. Snippet code itself is React-escaped; AI previews are unsafe (E02). Hydration failures, actual bundle sizes, contrast ratios, N+1 query totals and 10+ editor throughput remain unmeasured; no numbers invented. Frontend uses no SWR cache, so SWR-specific bugs are inapplicable; local projection/cache bugs are B01/B02/H02.\n\nREST errors mostly use {error}, SSE uses data error frames, Socket.io mixes code/message with silent validation drops. Health/readiness and shutdown exist, but readiness omits Redis/worker and shutdown has no deadline/reentrancy guard or awaited HTTP drain; exercise long-lived streams and Redis outage before asserting shutdown reliability. Workspaces/columns cascade-delete child content by schema; backup/restore testing and deletion confirmation must precede production destructive operations.\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\nSee `audit-evidence/commands.json`, `retry-commands.json`, verbatim *.log and audit JSON. Initial attempts encountered sandbox DNS/port restrictions and missing generated Prisma types; elevated retries are authoritative. No tests were skipped or edited to make results pass; the existing E2E suite skips itself when fixtures are absent. Screenshot outcomes and authentication blocks are listed in `ui/before/README.md`. Runtime limitations and human actions are in PROGRESS.md.\n'
D.joinpath('AUDIT.md').write_text(text)
D.joinpath('audit-evidence/findings.json').write_text(json.dumps(F,indent=2))
print(counts, len(F))
